# Monorepo Commands

## Backend (Java/Vert.x)

```bash
cd backend/server && mvn clean install        # build + test
cd backend/server && mvn verify               # tests + checkstyle
cd backend/pulse-s3-archiver && mvn verify    # Kafka→Parquet→S3 archiver (optional)
```

## Frontend (React/TypeScript)

```bash
corepack enable                               # First-time only (Yarn 4)
cd pulse-ui && yarn install && yarn start     # dev server on :3000
cd pulse-ui && yarn build                     # production build
cd pulse-ui && yarn lint                      # ESLint
```

## AI Agent (Python/Google ADK — Docker)

```bash
cd pulse_ai && cp .env.example .env           # first time — set GOOGLE_API_KEY
cd pulse_ai && ./setup.sh                     # build + start (Docker, port 8000)
cd pulse_ai && ./setup.sh logs                # tail logs
cd pulse_ai && ./setup.sh stop                # stop
```

## Docker (full stack)

```bash
cd deploy && ./scripts/quickstart.sh              # build + start all (includes pulse-ai-agent)
cd deploy && ./scripts/build.sh [ui|server|cron|capture|ingestion|heatmap|heatmap-ingestion|s3-archiver|ai|all] [--no-cache]
cd deploy && ./scripts/start.sh [-d|--detach] [--build] [--no-cache]
cd deploy && ./scripts/stop.sh [-v] [ai|server|...]
cd deploy && ./scripts/logs.sh [service]         # e.g. ai, server, mysql
```

To discover running services and their actual ports:
```bash
docker ps --format "table {{.Names}}\t{{.Ports}}\t{{.Status}}"
```

## Key Ports

| Service | Port | Health |
|---------|------|--------|
| pulse-server | 8080 | `/healthcheck` |
| pulse-ui (local `yarn start`) | 3000 | `/healthcheck.txt` |
| pulse-ai-agent (deploy stack or standalone `pulse_ai`) | 8000 | `curl -sf http://localhost:8000/health` |
| alerts-cron | 4000 | `/healthcheck` |
| ClickHouse | 8123 (HTTP), 9000 (native) | `SELECT 1` |
| MySQL | 3307 | `mysqladmin ping` |
| OpenFGA | 8180 (HTTP), 8181 (gRPC), 3001 (playground) | `/healthz` |
| OTEL Collector | 4317/4318, 13133 (health) | — |
| Optional Prometheus + Tempo + Grafana (`deploy/observability-otel-prometheus-tempo/`) | OTLP **14317/14318** (conflicts with Vector profile on same host), Grafana **3310**, Prometheus **9091** | separate `docker compose`; see folder `README.md` |
| Kafka (session replay) | 9092 | broker (no HTTP health in table) |
| MinIO (dev S3) | 9100 (API), 9101 (console) | — |
| pulse-session-capture | 3400 | `/healthcheck` |
| pulse-s3-archiver | — *(no host port in default compose)* | in-container `http://localhost:5000/healthcheck` (compose; HTTP may be unimplemented) |

## Never commit `.env` files. Use `.env.example` as template.
